
=========================================================
COMPLETE DOCKER + DOCKER COMPOSE NOTES
FOR BACKEND ENGINEERING
=========================================================

=========================================================
1. WHAT IS DOCKER?
=========================================================

Docker ek platform hai jo applications ko isolated
environment me run karta hai.

Is isolated environment ko bolte hain:

CONTAINER

Container ek lightweight mini-computer ki tarah hota hai.

Uske andar:
- application
- libraries
- dependencies
- runtime
- configs

sab hota hai.

=========================================================
2. WHY DOCKER WAS CREATED?
=========================================================

Before Docker:

Developer ke machine me:
- different software versions
- dependency conflicts
- setup issues

Example:

Developer A:
Node v18

Developer B:
Node v20

Application break ho sakti hai.

Docker solve karta hai:

"Works same everywhere"

=========================================================
3. WHAT IS A CONTAINER?
=========================================================

Container:
- lightweight
- isolated
- portable

environment hota hai.

Container me:
- OS layer
- software
- dependencies

hote hain.

=========================================================
4. CONTAINER VS VIRTUAL MACHINE
=========================================================

Virtual Machine:
- full operating system
- heavy
- slow

Container:
- lightweight
- fast
- shared kernel

Isi liye Docker popular hai.

=========================================================
5. WHAT IS DOCKER IMAGE?
=========================================================

Image = blueprint/template

Container = running instance of image

Example:

Image:
redis:7

Container:
running Redis server

=========================================================
6. WHAT IS DOCKER HUB?
=========================================================

Docker Hub ek online registry hai.

Yaha se images download hoti hain.

Example:

redis
mongo
node
nginx

=========================================================
7. WHAT IS DOCKER COMPOSE?
=========================================================

Docker Compose multiple containers ko ek saath manage karta hai.

Example:

Project needs:
- Node backend
- Redis
- MongoDB

Compose sabko ek command me run karega.

=========================================================
8. WHY DOCKER COMPOSE?
=========================================================

Without compose:

Har service manually start karo.

With compose:

docker compose up

Bas.

=========================================================
9. WHAT IS docker-compose.yml?
=========================================================

Ye infrastructure configuration file hoti hai.

Yaha define hota hai:

- services
- ports
- volumes
- environment variables
- networks

Matlab:

Infrastructure as Code

=========================================================
10. YOUR FILE EXPLANATION
=========================================================

services:
  redis:
    image: redis:7-alpine
    container_name: redis
    ports:
      - "6379:6379"
    command: ["redis-server", "--appendonly", "yes"]
    volumes:
      - redis-data:/data

  mongo:
    image: mongo:7
    container_name: chai-aur-mongo
    ports:
      - "27017:27017"
    environment:
      MONGO_INITDB_DATABASE: chai_aur_redis
    volumes:
      - mongo-data:/data/db

volumes:
  redis-data:
  mongo-data:

=========================================================
11. WHAT IS services?
=========================================================

services:
ke andar hum define karte hain:

Kaunse containers run honge.

Tumhare case me:
- Redis
- MongoDB

=========================================================
12. REDIS SERVICE
=========================================================

redis:

Redis container define kar raha hai.

=========================================================
13. IMAGE
=========================================================

image: redis:7-alpine

Meaning:

Docker Hub se:
Redis version 7 download karo.

Alpine:
lightweight Linux.

Small size.
Fast startup.

=========================================================
14. CONTAINER NAME
=========================================================

container_name: redis

Container ka custom naam.

Otherwise Docker random naam deta.

=========================================================
15. PORT MAPPING
=========================================================

ports:
  - "6379:6379"

Format:

HOST_PORT:CONTAINER_PORT

Meaning:

Machine ka 6379
-> container ke 6379 se connect hoga.

=========================================================
16. WHY PORTS NEEDED?
=========================================================

Container isolated hota hai.

Without port mapping:
outside world access nahi kar paayega.

=========================================================
17. WHAT IS COMMAND?
=========================================================

command:
["redis-server", "--appendonly", "yes"]

Custom startup command.

=========================================================
18. WHAT IS APPENDONLY?
=========================================================

Redis normally RAM use karta hai.

RAM volatile hoti hai.

Server restart:
data gone.

appendonly yes:
Redis disk pe bhi save karega.

This is called:

AOF
(Append Only File)

=========================================================
19. WHAT IS VOLUME?
=========================================================

Volume persistent storage hota hai.

=========================================================
20. WHY VOLUME IMPORTANT?
=========================================================

Without volume:

Container delete
-> data delete

With volume:

Container delete
-> data safe

=========================================================
21. REDIS VOLUME
=========================================================

volumes:
  - redis-data:/data

/data
Redis ka internal storage path hai.

=========================================================
22. MONGO SERVICE
=========================================================

mongo:

MongoDB container define kar raha hai.

=========================================================
23. MONGO IMAGE
=========================================================

image: mongo:7

MongoDB version 7.

=========================================================
24. MONGO PORT
=========================================================

27017 MongoDB ka default port hai.

=========================================================
25. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
=========================================================

environment:
  MONGO_INITDB_DATABASE: chai_aur_redis

Container start hote time:
database create karega.

=========================================================
26. MONGO VOLUME
=========================================================

mongo-data:/data/db

MongoDB ka actual data yaha store hota hai.

=========================================================
27. GLOBAL VOLUMES
=========================================================

volumes:
  redis-data:
  mongo-data:

Persistent storage create karte hain.

=========================================================
